                <pb facs="ur_d7-1" n="1" xml:id="ur_d7-1"/>

                <head>UR–7. Editorial Note</head>
                <p>On October 20, 1958, two contracts of sale were signed transferring all of the
                    assets and liabilities of the two U.S. meatpacking plants, Swift and Armour, to
                    a workers’ cooperative known as Establecimientos <pb facs="1248" n="1160"
                        type="typeset" xml:id="pg1160"/> Frigorificos del Cerro S.A., Uruguayan Army
                    troops, who had been guarding the plants, were withdrawn on October 27,
                    1958.</p>
                <p>[illegible in the original]</p>
            </div>
